Package: ccva
Type: Package
Title: Climate Change Vulnerability Assessment with Constrained Latent Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Hassan", "Doosti", email = "hassan.doosti@mq.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A general framework for climate change vulnerability assessment
    (CCVA) of any species and any dataset. Variables are tagged as exposure,
    sensitivity or adaptive capacity; each component is computed from its own
    predictors by a chosen method; and the three components are combined into
    vulnerability. Methods range from the conventional weighted index of
    Ofori et al. (2017) <doi:10.1038/s41598-017-13245-y> to shape-constrained
    additive models, latent-variable structural equation models in which
    vulnerability is inferred from observable proxies, and penalised regression
    for high-dimensional predictors. Ecological knowledge enters as explicit
    constraints on predictors and on each component's role in the model.
    Diagnostics, validation against observed outcomes, bootstrap and
    weight-based uncertainty, and plots for every step are included.
